// mod.rut — THE UI-FRAMEWORK PACKAGE (the two-package law): everything
// the biz code speaks THROUGH but never spells — the atom store
// machinery (Store, Source, Derived, Mutation), the t1 widget
// framework (the Widget type, the lowering table, the keyed diff),
// and the component vocabulary. ONE directory, ONE module, a
// FILE-MODULE TREE: this root carries the surface law and declares
// the children; the tiers keep the framework's private tables private
// for real — `pub` crosses packages, `pub(pkg)` shares inside ui,
// plain private stays in the declaring file.
//
// THE TREE (declarations are the graph — each child is `NAME/mod.rut`):
//   store/       §1 the atom store — the machinery
//   widget/      §2 the widget type
//   lowering/    §3 the lowering table
//   diff/        §4 the diff core
//   components/  §5 the component vocabulary
//
// THE STORE'S SURFACE (tur's law, ported — github.com/hpp2334/tur: the
// app never touches a store object; atoms and mutations are values the
// app and the widgets pass around; a component's onClick IS a
// mutation). MINTING and OBSERVABILITY live on the store; the two
// VERBS live on the handles, and the store's own are module-private:
//
//   store.source<T>(v)                  -> Source<T>     mint
//   store.source_str(v)                 -> Source<str>   mint (str lane)
//   store.derive<T>(fn (ctx) -> T)      -> Derived<T>    deps DISCOVERED
//   store.mutation<A, R>(fn (ctx, a) -> R) -> Mutation<A, R>
//   store.recompute_count() / store.deps_of(a)           observability
//   a.get()                             -> T             THE read (handle)
//   a.set(v)                            -> nil           the plain write (Source)
//   m.run(arg)                          -> R             the invocation (Mutation)
//   capture(m, arg)                     -> Mutation<str, opaque>
//     the event binding: a widget carries the composed mutation; the
//     framework runs it with the event's detail (tur's
//     `mutate((ctx, _ev) => act(ctx, index))`)
//
// The handles carry ids, seeds, and a PRIVATE store back-ref — the
// verbs are the handles' own pub methods, so biz never needs the store
// after boot; the store's plumbing members (atom_id/materialize) are
// module-private, so biz cannot spell them — and a Derived carries no
// set, so a derived is not writable AT THE TYPE LEVEL. The ctx forms
// are the app's only read/write spellings and they spell their shape:
// `ctx.get<V, K>(a)` / `ctx.set<R, A, K>(a, v)` (the fork's
// annotation law — the call site names the value type and the handle
// shape). A derive's ctx exposes get ONLY (derives are pure by
// construction); a mutation's ctx exposes get + set. Freshness is
// PULL-ON-READ: get() recomputes a stale derived at most once per
// write-set; there is no flush and no dirty set. The cycle guard (an
// in-flight set) returns because discovered edges admit cycles — a
// self-reading derive panics loud.
//
// The package exports GENERIC types (Source<T> and friends), so biz's
// unit and this unit compose with the graph's origin dedup — NOT the
// retired appkit concatenation.
//
// PURE of biz: nothing here names a todo, a list, or an app — the
// store is a DECOUPLED-BIZ design (the motivating pattern: the
// reactivity library over opaque cells).

pub mod store;
pub mod widget;
pub mod lowering;
pub mod diff;
pub mod components;

